.TH WSB 1 "November 2026" "WSB 1.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsb \- manage a BSD user-space environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wsb
.I command
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wsb
manages and provides access to a configured BSD environment from the host system.
Use a command to start or inspect the environment, open a shell, or manage a
dedicated server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
List available WSB commands.
.TP
.B start
Start the configured BSD environment.
.TP
.B shell
Open an interactive shell in the running BSD environment.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the BSD environment is running.
.TP
.B uninstall
Uninstall the configured BSD environment.
.TP
.B server-start
Start the configured dedicated server.
.TP
.B version
Display the WSB version.
.SH BSD COMMANDS
The BSD environment may provide commands such as
.BR freebsd-version (1),
.BR pkg (8),
.BR service (8),
.BR sysrc (8),
.BR bsdinstall (8),
.BR dmesg (8),
.BR jls (8),
and
.BR jexec (8).
Availability depends on the configured environment.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wsb help
List available WSB commands.
.TP
.B wsb start
Start the configured BSD environment.
.TP
.B wsb shell
Open a shell in the running environment.
.TP
.B wsb status
Check whether the environment is running.
.TP
.B wsb version
Display the WSB version.
.SH VERSION
WSB 1.1.3